  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On the road linking Gassin to Saint-Tropez, Le Treizain beach offers an open view of the gulf, with Saint-Tropez and Sainte-Maxime in the background. It is one of the three beaches of the town of Gassin, with free access, described as a "nature beach" by the tourist office.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Gassin tourist office lists "animals accepted" for Le Treizain beach, without specifying a leash requirement or a ban period; we have not read a municipal bylaw. The beach appears in the list of dog-friendly beaches of the Gulf of Saint-Tropez published by Grimaud Tourisme. Keep your dog on a leash, pick up his waste and follow the signs. Access is free.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: arrive late in the afternoon to enjoy the view of the gulf with your dog, when the light on Saint-Tropez is at its best.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p><a href="/en/fiche-plage-moune-gassin">La Moune beach</a>, right next door, and the village of Gassin inland easily round off the outing.</p>
